{"name":"Praying Mantis","hex":"#a5be8f","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"praying mantis","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various predatory, cannibalistic insects of the order Mantodea that have a prayer-like stance.","European mantis: a mantid of the species Mantis religiosa."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/praying_mantis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Praying Mantis (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Praying Mantis are an English rock band. Originally part of the new wave of British heavy metal, they pursued a musical direction more AOR/melodic rock-sounding than their contemporaries Iron Maiden and Saxon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/PrayingMantisSRF2010.jpg/330px-PrayingMantisSRF2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Praying_Mantis_(band)"},{"title":"Mantis","blocks":[{"text":"Mantises are an order (Mantodea) of insects that contains over 2,400 species in about 460 genera in 33 families. The largest family is the Mantidae (\"mantids\"). Mantises are distributed worldwide in temperate and tropical habitats. They have triangular heads with bulging eyes supported on flexible necks. Their elongated bodies may or may not have wings, but all mantodeans have forelegs that are greatly enlarged and adapted for catching and gripping prey; their upright posture, while remaining stationary with forearms folded, resembling a praying posture, has led to the common name praying mantis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Mantis_%28European%29.jpg/330px-Mantis_%28European%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mantis"},{"title":"Shades of green","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color green may differ in hue, chroma or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints 